;GIAT ADR
;The ADR is an interesting firearm with two pistol grips. The initial prototypes had two triggers; one trigger for semi-automatic fire and another for fully automatic fire. Ammunition was fed from a 20-round detachable box magazine. The ADR could also hold an extra magazine in the pistol grip. It had cyclic rate of 300 to 1,000 rounds per minute.
;Tatara Pin Pusher
;Brought to you by the one and only Kogasa Tatara, the Pin Pusher is her take on the well-known ArmTeck MR-70 rifle. It feels a lot like a regular MR-70, just that it feels like it's freshly made. Comes in select-fire with Atare markings on the fire selector. Receiver is marked with an umbrella with a tongue sticking out. Underneeth is the markings \"Tatara Pin Pusher 5.56mm小銃\".
;Tatara Pin Pusher A1
;Kogasa Tatara's first revision of the Pin Pusher rifle. You can hear some sort of electrical hum. Comes in select-fire with SAFE, SEMI, and FULL markings on the fire selector. Receiver is marked with an umbrella with a tongue sticking out. Underneeth is the markings \"Tatara Pin Pusher A1, CAL 5.56x45\".
;Tatara Pin Pusher A2
;This model of the Pin Pusher includes a tactical umbrella along with several improvements to it's design manufacture. The umbrella can be used as a ballistic shield against bullets and spells.
